    board(pm): file CF-190 — the control host's SSH publish path strands commits
    
    Measured this tick: `git push origin main` in the registered checkout answers
    `git@github.com: Permission denied (publickey)`, so a lane that follows "push after every
    commit" strands its work; the CF-071 landing sat unpublished from 09:34Z to 09:44Z and the
    local `origin/main` tracking ref was 17 commits stale. The HTTPS rewrite through the host's
    gh credential helper is the only transport that worked here (parity 0 0 after `caf4364`).
    
    Row CF-190 carries the reproduction as its probe and asks for one documented publish command
    plus a selftest arm that fails when push authentication is broken. No doc or row covered this
    class before (census against CF-003 deploy keys and CF-060 lane identity found neither).
    
