red admission mode, or keeps the historical `tasks` reading explicitly dated to the run that measured it (tick id and/or tip) and labels it historical, so no present-tense live claim is contradicted by the recipe beneath it.\n2. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` and `scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK` at the fix commit.", "probe": "cd /home/kara/code-factory 2>/dev/null; s=$(mktemp -d); awk '/^\\($/{f=1} f{print} /^\\)$/{if(f){exit}}' README.md > \"$s/census.sh\"; bash -n \"$s/census.sh\" && bash \"$s/census.sh\" | grep -E '^(19|.*code-factory-duckbrain )'; echo \"readme_claim=$(grep -c 'code-factory-duckbrain admission=tasks' README.md)\"; rm -rf \"$s\"", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:28:59Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:28:59Z"}
 {"id": "CF-189", "title": "P3 — OPERATIONS.md marks destroy BLOCKED and forbids guessing bunker flags, while node-create.sh prints an exact `bunker destroy` line that was measured working", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-04 by the code-factory-duckbrain-dogfood tick code-factory-duckbrain-dogfood-2026-11-04-08-40-09 (third execution) at origin/main d65adf9, on a real bunker host (server bunker-mvp) and a real public repo (https://github.com/github/gitignore), with the real crier on :8767 reachable from the node (layer-00 `PASS reach:.../health — 200`). `scripts/node-create.sh --project myrepo --repo https://github.com/github/gitignore --harness hermes --ttl 1h` reached NODE INCOMPLETE and its failure path printed: `cleanup required: bunker destroy node-myrepo-042342 --server bunker-mvp` (scripts/node-create.sh:55, incomplete()). That exact line was then run as printed: `bunker destroy node-myrepo-042342 --server bunker-mvp` -> 'Destroying agent node-myrepo-042342 (home 435.2 MB; archiving before delete, deadline 12m0s)…' / 'Agent node-myrepo-042342 destroyed.' / 'Removed local SSH key /home/kara/.config/bunker/keys/node-myrepo-042342', rc=0, and `bunker list --server bunker-mvp` returned to the pre-run two agents. The runbook says the opposite twice: docs/OPERATIONS.md:167 'There is no checked-in command or measured procedure for renewing a bunker agent TTL, destroying an agent … These steps are BLOCKED / NOT YET. Do not guess bunker CLI flags' and :173 'No teardown script is currently tracked … teardown is a manual, operator-owned, BLOCKED change—not a guessed command.' So the one path a new user is told to walk hands them a command their runbook says is unmeasured and forbidden, and the operator cannot tell whether following it is supported. Distinct from the pending CF-150 (nothing stages the gateway auth block, so create can never pass) and CF-179 (the success line prints a literal /home/<uid>): this row is that the documented lifecycle state of destroy is contradicted by the shipped script.", "acceptance_criteria": "0. Reproduce: with CRIER_URL and BUNKER_SERVER set and no node inference key, run the documented create; the failure path prints `cleanup required: bunker destroy <agent> --server <server>`, and running that line destroys the agent (rc=0, archive-then-delete, SSH key removed) as measured above.\n1. Document and script agree: either docs/OPERATIONS.md §8 records destroy as a MEASURED step (naming the run, the date, the archive-before-delete behaviour and the ~435 MB home it archived), or scripts/node-create.sh stops printing a command the runbook forbids. Renew, rebuild and full teardown may stay BLOCKED, but they are separated from destroy instead of sharing its verdict.\n2. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` and `scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK` at the fix commit.", "probe": "grep -n 'cleanup required' scripts/node-create.sh; grep -n 'BLOCKED / NOT YET\\|not a guessed command' docs/OPERATIONS.md | head -4; echo 'measured 2026-11-04: bunker destroy node-myrepo-042342 --server bunker-mvp -> rc=0, \"Agent node-myrepo-042342 destroyed.\", home 435.2 MB archived'", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:28:59Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:28:59Z"}
+{"id":"CF-190","title":"P4 — the configured SSH remote does not authenticate on the fleet control host, so a lane following \"push after commit\" strands its commits and reads a stale origin/main","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-04 by the code-factory-duckbrain-pm lane on the fleet control host. The registered checkout's `origin` is `git@github.com:coding-hermes/code-factory.git`, so the fleet-wide instruction \"after ANY commit run `git push origin <branch>`\" resolves to an SSH push — which this host cannot perform from an unattended session: `git push origin main` answers `git@github.com: Permission denied (publickey)` (the session's ssh-agent holds no identities and `~/.ssh/code-github.key` is refused), and `git fetch` fails the same way, so a lane's own `origin/main` tracking ref silently stays stale (this pass read a 17-commit-stale ref until it used `git ls-remote`). Consequence measured today: the CF-071 worker's commits `3e6ac40`, `779ab4f`, `1d632d9` and its board closeout `48e1501` sat unpublished from 09:34Z until 09:44Z, and the checkout read `origin/main...HEAD = 0 2` against a ref that named a tip nine commits behind the real remote. The only transport that works here is the HTTPS rewrite through the host's authenticated `gh` credential helper: `git -c url.https://github.com/.insteadOf=git@github.com: push origin main` pushed `caf4364` and `293f7ec` and parity went to `0 0`. GitHub also answered `Internal Server Error` on two consecutive pushes before accepting a third, so a single push attempt is not evidence of a transport failure either. No tracked doc names a supported push path: `grep -n -i 'push|ssh|credential|https' docs/OPERATIONS.md` returns only node-side clone/credential text, `AGENTS.md` carries no push instruction, and `grep -rn 'push' tests/selftest.sh` has no arm that would fail when push auth is broken. Distinct from CF-003 (per-repo deploy keys for cloning on nodes) and from CF-060 (lane_target code identity): this is the control host's publish path for the repo itself. Escape hatch used this tick: HTTPS rewrite with the gh helper, disclosed in the landing messages.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree (from the repo root): `git push --dry-run origin HEAD:main` exits non-zero and prints `git@github.com: Permission denied (publickey)`, while `git -c url.https://github.com/.insteadOf=git@github.com: push --dry-run origin HEAD:main` reaches the remote and prints an up-to-date or would-push line.\n1. One tracked doc (AGENTS.md or docs/OPERATIONS.md) names exactly one supported unattended publish command, states that it uses the host's authenticated credential helper, carries no credential in argv, and quotes the measured exit code it produces on a green run.\n2. A shipped check FAILS with a named row when push authentication is unavailable, so a lane cannot report a landed commit while its push silently died: `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints a `FAIL  push-transport — …` row (never a bare PASS) for a fixture whose push is refused, and a `PASS  push-transport — …` row for a fixture whose push succeeds in the same run.\n3. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` at the fixed tip.","probe":"set +e; ssh_out=$(git push --dry-run origin HEAD:main 2>&1); ssh_rc=$?; https_out=$(git -c \"url.https://github.com/.insteadOf=git@github.com:\" push --dry-run origin HEAD:main 2>&1); https_rc=$?; ssh_line=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$ssh_out\" | grep -m1 'Permission denied' || printf '%s\\n' \"$ssh_out\" | tail -1); https_line=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$https_out\" | tail -1); printf 'ssh_rc=%s %s\\nhttps_rc=%s %s\\n' \"$ssh_rc\" \"$ssh_line\" \"$https_rc\" \"$https_line\"","created_at":"2026-11-04T09:47:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T09:47:26Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"e20cddf4572d687d42df268fabd41b204dba7949d2dc5efe25c6dcf95ca380f7"}}
